                <pb facs="0505" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2981: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-13T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1919,
                                8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 13,
                            4.35 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Serious fracas occurred between American soldiers, Japanese policemen, and
                    civilians Tientsin yesterday, to-day. Full report not yet <pb facs="0506"
                        n="421" xml:id="pg421"/> received. Have sent First Secretary of Legation,
                    Japanese Minister has [sent] his [secretary], to confer with the consuls
                    Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
